<BaseLayout title="Acupressure for Back Pain: Best Points" description="Learn how to use acupressure for back pain relief. Guide to BL40, BL60, GB21, and other points for lower and upper back pain." breadcrumbs={[{ "label": "Home", "href": "/" }, { "label": "Conditions", "href": "/conditions" }, { "label": "Acupressure for Back Pain", "href": "/conditions/acupressure-for-back-pain" }]} datePublished="2025-04-01" dateModified="2026-06-01" articleSchema={true}>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 lg:px-6"><h1 class="mb-4">Acupressure for Back Pain: Best Points for Lasting Relief</h1><p class="text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400 text-lg mb-8">Acupressure targets the root causes of back pain by releasing muscle tension, improving circulation, and activating the body's natural pain relief mechanisms.</p><section id="bl40" class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">1. BL40 (Weizhong) - Middle of the Crook</h2><p class="mb-3">BL40 is the most important acupressure point for lower back pain. Located in the crease behind the knee, this point has a direct meridian connection to the lower back.</p><p class="mb-3"><strong>Location:</strong> In the center of the crease behind the knee (popliteal fossa).</p><p class="mb-3"><strong>Technique:</strong> While sitting with your leg bent, use both thumbs to press into the center of the knee crease. Hold for 1-2 minutes per leg.</p></section><section id="bl60" class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">2. BL60 (Kunlun) - Kunlun Mountains</h2><p class="mb-3">BL60 is effective for lower back pain, especially pain that radiates down the leg (sciatica).</p><p class="mb-3"><strong>Location:</strong> In the depression between the outer ankle bone and the Achilles tendon.</p><p class="mb-3"><strong>Technique:</strong> Press firmly into the hollow behind the outer ankle. Hold for 1-2 minutes per leg.</p></section><section id="gb21" class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">3. GB21 (Jianjing) - Shoulder Well</h2><p class="mb-3">GB21 is the primary point for upper back and shoulder tension. It releases tightness that often contributes to upper back pain.</p><p class="mb-3"><strong>Location:</strong> At the midpoint of the shoulder, directly above the nipple line, in the belly of the trapezius muscle.</p><p class="mb-3"><strong>Technique:</strong> Use your opposite hand to press deeply into the shoulder muscle. Hold for 1-2 minutes per side.</p></section><section id="bl23" class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">4. BL23 (Shenshu) - Kidney Shu</h2><p class="mb-3">BL23 supports kidney energy, which TCM associates with lower back strength. It is excellent for chronic lower back pain with fatigue.</p><p class="mb-3"><strong>Location:</strong> On the lower back, 1.5 finger-widths from the spine at the level of the second lumbar vertebra.</p></section><section id="routine" class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Back Pain Relief Routine</h2><ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2 text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300"><li>Start with BL40 (2 minutes each leg) to open the back meridian</li><li>Move to BL60 (1 minute each ankle) for sciatic pain</li><li>Press GB21 (1 minute each shoulder) for upper back tension</li><li>End with BL23 (2 minutes each side) for lower back support</li></ol></section><section id="evidence" class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Scientific Evidence</h2><p class="mb-3">A 2023 systematic review of 14 studies found acupressure significantly reduced chronic lower back pain intensity by an average of 45%. Combined with conventional treatment, acupressure improved mobility and reduced pain medication use.</p></section><hr class="my-8"><div class="bg-stone-100 dark:bg-stone-800 rounded-lg p-6 text-sm text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400"><p><strong>Medical Disclaimer:</strong> Seek medical evaluation for back pain accompanied by numbness, weakness, bowel/bladder changes, or if pain persists more than 2 weeks.</p></div></article>
